  "Question": "A haunted house has six windows. In how many ways can Georgie the Ghost enter the house by one window and leave by a different window?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\)",
    "B": "\\(15\\)",
    "C": "\\(18\\)",
    "D": "\\(30\\)",
    "E": "\\(36\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "First choose the entrance window, which can be any of the \\(6\\) windows. For each entrance, Georgie has \\(5\\) exit choices because he cannot leave through the window he entered. Every valid trip has exactly one entrance and one exit, so these choices include every trip exactly once. Reversing the entrance and exit gives a different trip. Thus there are\n\\[\n6\\cdot5=30\n\\]\nways, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
